// Shared scaffolding for EVERY reducer-shaped Cadenza guest (design/cadenza-platform.md §3) — not just the §9
// checkers. Every reducer guest repeated the same reducer-interface plumbing: the `Outcome` return sum, the
// `Error` sum, and the two inert `on-response` / `on-notification` handlers a guest that only reacts to
// delivered messages needs but never varies. This module owns them so a guest keeps only its own `on-message`
// logic and re-exports the shared handlers. (The §9 checkers layer their check/verdict machinery — respond,
// the log-iteration combinators — on top of this in checker-lib.cdz.)
//
// Composed into a guest via its `libs` manifest (the mkCadenzaGuest multi-file path). Self-contained: it
// imports nothing, so a plain reducer that only needs the scaffolding does not drag in the checker schemas.

// How a fold ends (design §7): keep the session running for the next event, or close it with a typed reason.
type Outcome = | Continue | Close(Record(schema: Bytes, reason: Bytes))

// The runtime message-fold error sum (a reducer's response `answer` is `Result(payload, Error)`, §4). Declared
// here so a guest need not re-declare it; the world-export boundary reads it when synthesizing the response
// parameter type of `on-response` below, and a guest that builds an `answer` (e.g. deliver-response) imports it.
type Error = | Timeout | MissingHandler | SchemaViolation | Faulted

// The inert on-response / on-notification a message-only reducer shares — no requests, just continue. The
// parameters are annotated to their concrete world shapes (response = {contract, token, answer:
// Result(payload, Error)}, notification = {contract, payload}) so the world-export boundary can fix them
// against this module's Outcome/Error rather than requiring the guest to declare its own (the CDZ0201
// parameter-synthesis remedy). A guest with inert handlers re-exports these directly; a guest whose handler
// actually reacts (e.g. reducer-onresponse-cdz emits on-response) keeps its own and re-exports only the inert one.
def on-response(_resp: Record(contract: Bytes, token: Bytes, answer: Result(Bytes, Error))) =
  { requests = [], outcome = Outcome.Continue }
def on-notification(_note: Record(contract: Bytes, payload: Bytes)) =
  { requests = [], outcome = Outcome.Continue }

export { Outcome.*, Error.*, on-response, on-notification }
